  "body": "This commit resolves an off-by-one error in the specification for index assignment on HTMLOptionsCollection when the target index is greater than the current length of the collection.\n\nFixes #11905\n\nThis is a spec bug all browsers behave this way already.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11932/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2025, 1:02 PM UTC (a2c7f90)\">/acknowledgements.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11932/0cb9486...a2c7f90/acknowledgements.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2025, 1:02 PM UTC (a2c7f90)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11932/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2025, 1:02 PM UTC (a2c7f90)\">/common-dom-interfaces.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/11932/0cb9486...a2c7f90/common-dom-interfaces.html\" title=\"Last updated on Nov 20, 2025, 1:02 PM UTC (a2c7f90)\">diff</a> )",
